  "timepicker": {},
  "timezone": "Europe/Oslo",
  "title": "SLA - Service Owners",
  "uid": "altinn-uptime-sla-service-owners",
  "weekStart": "",
  "description": "Per-service-owner availability of the Altinn apps hosts (<org>.apps.altinn.no and <org>.apps.tt02.altinn.no) in admin-prod-obs-amw, with an SLA measured per calendar month (default range: last 30 days; pick e.g. 'Previous month' in the time picker for a calendar month). Prod: 99.9 %, 24/7, from altinn:probe_success_1m. tt02: 99.8 % of all hours in the month, but only downtime inside the operating period counts (the recording rule counts Mon–Fri 05:00–19:00 UTC. This covers 07:00–20:00 Norwegian time in both summer time (07:00–21:00) and winter time (06:00–20:00), so up to one extra hour per day is counted), from altinn:probe_success_tt02_business_hours_1m. The base rule altinn:probe_success:max_by_instance runs every 5 minutes and takes max by instance over the blackbox-http-ipv4/ipv6-kuberneteswrapper jobs, so a host counts as up when at least one blackbox-exporter pod reaches it over IPv4 or IPv6. The _1m rules run every minute but read that 5-minute base, so each series holds one 0/1 sample per 5 minutes. Planned maintenance is not excluded. Filter with the Customer variable. Datasource UIDs are pinned rather than templated so the panels cannot silently bind to the wrong Prometheus datasource."
}
